  "title": "Provider-neutral tracker seam with a GitHub Issues adapter",
  "summary": "Adds a new `tracker` module that defines the provider-neutral `Tracker` trait (read ready items, write state, write recap, report capabilities) plus the ready rule, the run-finishing writes, and an in-memory test double. Alongside it, `github_tracker` implements that trait over the installed `gh` CLI: pure functions build each GraphQL argv and JSON payload, pure parsers read each response, and a `GhRunner` seam (real, timeout-bounded, or scripted) executes one `gh` invocation per request. Nothing in the existing engine is rewired yet; this change lands the seam and its first adapter, with tests covering the fake run, the real runner, and provider-neutrality of the tracker source.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
